Important discovery: The live CrankNicolsonFEM class (line 318) is ALREADY the fixed version: `self.B = Tridiagonal(h/6 - c/h, 2h/3 + 2c/h, h/6 - c/h, m)` with comment "a first version used M - cK on the RHS and grew linearly". So the fix is in the live code, and the triage's claim is documented in a code comment as well.

But note something interesting: the triage says the root cause was the wrong RHS `(M - cK) psi^{n-1}` while B itself = M + cK. The live code's `B` has off-diagonal `h/6 - c/h`. With h=0.1, c/h = (0.5*dt²)/h; for dr=0.2, c/h = 0.5*(0.1²)/0.2=0.025; h/6=0.0333; so B off-diag = 0.0083 > 0. Fine.

