Careful: B = M + cK has off-diagonal h/6 - c/h and diagonal 2h/3 + 2c/h. M - cK would have off-diagonal h/6 + c/h and diagonal 2h/3 - 2c/h. The triage says the buggy RHS was `(M - cK)`, i.e. B_wrong = M - c*K. So:
```python
c=0.5*dt**2; q=c/h
self.B_wrong = Tridiagonal(h/6 + q, 2h/3 - 2q, h/6 + q, m)
```
Then step:
```python
rhs = 2*self.M.matvec(self.psi[1:-1]) - self.B_wrong.matvec(self.psi_prev[1:-1])
nxt[1:-1] = self.B.solve(rhs)   # left side still (M + cK)
```
That matches the described bug: left (M+cK), right 2M psi^n - (M-cK) psi^{n-1}.

